discussion_comments.comment_body:
The regexes anchor with `^` and `$`. In a live IDE session, `toolResult` often carries a trailing `\n` (Kiro's JSON serialization doesn't strip it). With the current code, `"Created the intent.md file.\n"` matches nothing, `extractWrittenPath` returns `""`, and the audit-and-sensors pipeline silently no-ops — the exact same symptom this PR fixes, just triggered by whitespace instead of a relative path. A `.trim()` before matching makes it resilient. Consider adding a `\n`-suffixed case to t188 as well.

```suggestion
function extractWrittenPath(toolResult: string): string {
  const t = toolResult.trim();
  let m = t.match(/^Created the (.+) file\.$/);
  if (m) return m[1];
  m = t.match(/^Replaced text in (.+)$/);
  if (m) return m[1];
  m = t.match(/^Appended the text to the (.+) file\.$/);
  if (m) return m[1];
  return "";
}
```

